<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Argyle International Airport</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2017</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Argyle International Airport is the main airport of Saint Vincent and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grenadines">Grenadines</a>, on the south-east coast of Saint Vincent. Built over about a decade with help from countries including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> and Venezuela, it opened in February 2017, replacing the small E. T. Joshua Airport at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arno">Arnos</a> Vale. Its long runway allows direct flights from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/argyle-international-airport.jpg" alt="Argyle International Airport" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dylanwill · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Argyle_Terminal_Building.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
